---
import MainLayout from '@layouts/MainLayout.astro';
---

<MainLayout
  title="Cognituum | Jose Vigil"
  description="Your engineering decisions outrank the model's — a research initiative into cognitive continuity for AI-assisted workflows."
  image="../images/jose_vigil.png"
>
  <section>
    <div class="section-label">
      <span class="sec-num">§</span>Systems · Cognituum
    </div>

    <div class="project-hero reveal">
      <h1 class="sec-h2">Cognituum</h1>
      <p class="project-tagline">Your engineering decisions outrank the model's.</p>
    </div>

    <table class="spec-table reveal">
      <tr>
        <td>Role</td>
        <td>Founder (sole founder)</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Focus</td>
        <td>Current primary focus, full-time</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Status</td>
        <td>Active development · Early access opening to a small group of senior engineers and developers</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Output</td>
        <td>Whitepaper / framework specification, in progress</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Website</td>
        <td><a href="https://cognituum.com" class="text-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener">cognituum.com</a></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>GitHub</td>
        <td><a href="https://github.com/cognituum" class="text-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener">github.com/cognituum</a></td>
      </tr>
    </table>

    <blockquote class="pull-quote reveal">
      Every session with an AI model starts a negotiation you already won last week. Cognituum keeps your engineering call as the final one — versioned, signed, remembered. You decide once. It stays decided.
    </blockquote>

    <p class="body-text reveal">
      Most AI tooling today is episodic — each session starts over, and context, intent and institutional knowledge get lost between tools, sessions and providers. You explain the architecture, the constraints, the reasoning — and the model forgets, session after session. That costs tokens spent re-establishing context that should have simply persisted, and judgment quality lost when a model quietly overrides a call that should have stayed yours.
    </p>
    <p class="body-text reveal">
      Cognituum is built on a simple inversion: your engineering decisions outrank the model's. Once you decide something, it's captured and enforced, not re-negotiated tool by tool. It's provider-agnostic by design — Claude, Codex, Gemini, whatever you use, your judgment sits above all of them, not inside one of them.
    </p>
    <p class="body-text reveal">
      We're in active development, opening early access to a small group of senior engineers and developers before public availability.
    </p>

    <div class="sys-tags reveal">
      <span class="sys-tag">Continuity</span>
      <span class="sys-tag">Provider-Agnostic</span>
      <span class="sys-tag">Local Knowledge</span>
      <span class="sys-tag">Whitepaper</span>
    </div>

    <div class="sys-links reveal">
      <a href="https://cognituum.com" class="sys-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Get early access →</a>
      <a href="https://github.com/cognituum" class="sys-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub →</a>
      <a href="/#systems" class="sys-link">← Back to Systems</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</MainLayout>

<style>
.project-hero {
  margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
}
.project-hero .sec-h2 {
  margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
}
.project-tagline {
  font-size: 1.1rem;
  font-style: italic;
  color: var(--ink-2);
  max-width: 600px;
}

/* ── SPEC TABLE (verbatim from the original Paper & Ink mockup) ── */
.spec-table {
  width: 100%;
  border-collapse: collapse;
  font-size: 0.82rem;
  margin: 2rem 0;
}
.spec-table tr { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule-light); }
.spec-table tr:first-child { border-top: 2px solid var(--ink); }
.spec-table tr:last-child { border-bottom: 2px solid var(--rule); }
.spec-table td {
  padding: 0.55rem 1rem 0.55rem 0;
  color: var(--ink-2);
  line-height: 1.5;
}
.spec-table td:first-child {
  font-family: var(--mono);
  font-size: 0.6rem;
  letter-spacing: 0.1em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--ink-4);
  width: 160px;
}

/* ── TAGS / LINKS (same language as SystemsSection) ── */
.sys-tags {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 0.5rem;
  margin-top: 1.5rem;
}
.sys-tag {
  font-family: var(--mono);
  font-size: 0.52rem;
  letter-spacing: 0.12em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--ink-3);
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  padding-bottom: 1px;
}
.sys-links {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 1.5rem;
  margin-top: 1.5rem;
}
.sys-link {
  font-family: var(--mono);
  font-size: 0.6rem;
  letter-spacing: 0.14em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--red);
  text-decoration: none;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--red);
  padding-bottom: 1px;
  transition: opacity 0.2s;
}
.sys-link:hover { opacity: 0.65; }
</style>
